{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And the manner</b> of a ladder is to be a symbol, or it is among the kinds of derash. R. Solomon the Spaniard said that the ladder alludes to the supernal soul, and the angels of Elohim are thoughts of wisdom. And R. Isaac said that the reason of the ladder is that his prayer ascended upon it, and his salvation descended from the heavens. And these commentators did not see the prophecies of Zechariah and Amos and Jeremiah. And the meaning is by way of parable, for nothing is hidden from HaShem, and things below depend on those above, and it is as though there is a ladder between them, by which the angels ascend to make things known after they have walked about on the earth; likewise others are written as descending to fulfill the missions of HaShem, in the manner of a king with his attendants:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:10.430884173Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}